        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the incorrect assignment of `port_num` and `pkey_index` in the `get_new_pps` function. When the `qp_attr_mask` included `IB_QP_PORT` or `IB_QP_PKEY_INDEX`, the function was incorrectly using values from the old `qp_pps` instead of the current attributes from `qp_attr`. This led to inconsistencies and potential panics in certain configurations when the values were expected to be updated.

        Commit message:
        RDMA/core: Fix pkey and port assignment in get_new_pps

When port is part of the modify mask, then we should take it from the
qp_attr and not from the old pps. Same for PKEY. Otherwise there are
panics in some configurations:

